0e9e ferme \u00e0 17h, nous vous recommandons donc de profiter du mus\u00e9e d\u00e8s 14h15, avant la rencontre avec nos voisins \u00e0 15h15.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/sewermuseum.brussels\/news\/a-la-rencontre-de-nos-voisins-le-groene-phare\/","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700004755"},"sp":{"name":"\u00c0 la rencontre de nos voisins \u2013 Le Groene Phare","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/sewermuseum.brussels\/news\/a-la-rencontre-de-nos-voisins-le-groene-phare\/","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700004755"},"nl":{"name":"\u00c0 la rencontre de nos voisins \u2013 Le Groene Phare","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/sewermuseum.brussels\/news\/a-la-rencontre-de-nos-voisins-le-groene-phare\/","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700004755"}},"place":{"id":242977,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Bruxella 1238","address_street_name":"Rue de la Bourse","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"contact@boursebeurs.be","website":"https:\/\/www.boursebeurs.be\/fr\/bruxella-1238","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de la Bourse","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Am Fu\u00dfe der Br\u00fcsseler B\u00f6rse verbirgt sich eine kleine, aber ganz erstaunliche arch\u00e4ologische St\u00e4tte, die auch f\u00fcr die \u00d6ffentlichkeit zug\u00e4nglich ist. Es handelt sich um die Ruinen des Franziskanerordens, der in Br\u00fcssel ab 1238 erbaut wurde. Hier befindet sich auch das Grab des Herzogs Johann I. von Brabant. Das Fundament und verschiedene andere \u00dcberreste geben einen faszinierenden Einblick in einen weniger bekannten Teil der Br\u00fcsseler Stadtgschichte.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Bruxella 1238","address_street_name":"Rue de la Bourse","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"contact@boursebeurs.be","website":"https:\/\/www.boursebeurs.be\/fr\/bruxella-1238","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de la Bourse","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Bruxella 1238","address_street_name":"Beursstraat","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"contact@boursebeurs.be","website":"https:\/\/www.boursebeurs.be\/en\/bruxella-1238","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Beursstraat","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"Next to the stock exchange building, in the heart of Brussels, is a fascinating little archaeological site.  It contains the remains of the Franciscan monastery founded in Brussels in 1238 and the tomb of Duke John I of Brabant.  The foundations and various other objects offer a glimpse of an unknown side of the history of Brussels, and at the same time give a good idea of the different aspects of an archaeological dig.","description_print":null,"booking_url":"https:\/\/www.ticketing.brussels\/en\/tickets\/event-details.Bruxella-1238.4e2fe0b8-72e4-44c0-abcc-d72a3b0c5618","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Bruxella 1238","address_street_name":"Rue de la Bourse","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"contact@boursebeurs.be","website":"https:\/\/www.boursebeurs.be\/fr\/bruxella-1238","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de la Bourse","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Bruxella 1238","address_street_name":"Rue de la Bourse","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"contact@boursebeurs.be","website":"https:\/\/www.boursebeurs.be\/fr\/bruxella-1238","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de la Bourse","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Bruxella 1238","address_street_name":"Rue de la Bourse","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"contact@boursebeurs.be","website":"https:\/\/www.boursebeurs.be\/fr\/bruxella-1238","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de la Bourse","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Au pied de la Bourse, se cache un \u00e9tonnant petit site arch\u00e9ologique ouvert au public, au coeur de Bruxelles, celui-ci pr\u00e9sente les vestiges du Couvent de l'ordre franciscain \u00e9rig\u00e9 \u00e0 Bruxelles d\u00e8s 1238. On y trouve notamment le tombeau du Duc Jean Ier de Brabant. Les fondations et un mat\u00e9riel diversifi\u00e9 permettent de faire revivre un pan m\u00e9connu de l'histoire de Bruxelles, tout en laissant percevoir diff\u00e9rents aspects de la r\u00e9alit\u00e9 du m\u00e9tier d'arch\u00e9ologue.","description_print":null,"booking_url":"https:\/\/www.ticketing.brussels\/fr\/tickets\/event-details.Bruxella-1238.4e2fe0b8-72e4-44c0-abcc-d72a3b0c5618","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"Bruxella 1238","address_street_name":"Rue de la Bourse","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"contact@boursebeurs.be","website":"https:\/\/www.boursebeurs.be\/fr\/bruxella-1238","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de la Bourse","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"Bruxella 1238","address_street_name":"Beursstraat","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"contact@boursebeurs.be","website":"https:\/\/www.boursebeurs.be\/nl\/bruxella-1238","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Beursstraat","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"Aan de voet van de Beurs verbergt er zich een fascinerende archeologische site in het centrum van Brussel die de bezoekers een kijk geeft op de resten van het franciscaans klooster dat in Brussel vanaf 1238 werd opgericht. We vinden er ondermeer het graf van Hertog Jan I van Brabant. De funderingen en allerlei ander materiaal laten ons toe om een ongekend stukje uit de geschiedenis van Brussel te laten herleven en ons tegelijkertijd een goed beeld te geven van de verschillende aspecten van het beroep van archeoloog.","description_print":null,"booking_url":"https:\/\/www.ticketing.brussels\/nl\/tickets\/event-details.Bruxella-1238.4e2fe0b8-72e4-44c0-abcc-d72a3b0c5618","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"districts":{"list":[13],"translations":{"de":["Historisches Stadtzentrum"],"pt":[null],"en":["Historical Centre"],"it":["Centro storico"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Centre historique"],"sp":["Centro hist\u00f3rico"],"nl":["Historisch centrum"]}},"zones":{"list":[19],"translations":{"de":["Zentrum"],"pt":[null],"en":["Centre"],"it":["Centro"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Centre"],"sp":["Centro"],"nl":["Centrum"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":5373,"location":{"lat":50.8480633,"lon":4.3508541},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2024-09-11T10:29:20+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:18:35+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":231869,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Kanalisationsmuseum (Mus\u00e9e des \u00c9gouts)","address_street_name":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedesegouts.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 83","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Das Kanalisationsmuseum f\u00fchrt Sie hinab in die Unterwelten der Br\u00fcsseler Kanalisation. Entdecken Sie die Geheimnisse des faszinierenden, 400 Kilometer langen Labyrinths, das sich unter dem Br\u00fcsseler Stadtgebiet auftut. Tausende Kubikmeter Wasser flie\u00dfen t\u00e4glich durch die Br\u00fcsseler Abwasserkanalisation. Was mit ihnen geschieht, welche Wege sie nehmen, erfahren Sie im Kanalisationsmuseum - ein Museum mit vielen interessanten Details f\u00fcr Gro\u00df und Klein: Geschichtliches, Technisches und Am\u00fcsantes.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e des \u00c9gouts - Mus\u00e9es de la Ville de Bruxelles","address_street_name":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedesegouts.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 83","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Sewer Museum","address_street_name":"Octrooipaviljoen, Anderlechtsepoort","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.sewermuseum.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 83","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Octrooipaviljoen, Anderlechtsepoort","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"Why not visit the Brussels sewers and the Sewers museum during your next excursion in Brussels. A visit of Brussels' sewerage network - led by experienced guides or ex-workers - is extraordinary, full of surprises, but above all fascinating. The sewers have become vital to our way of life, so much so that it's hard to imagine what it was like before they existed. A visit of the Sewers Museum (and a real sewer!) is therefore an amazing, unusual and thrilling experience.\r\nBrussels' first sewerage network came into use in the 17th century, but they were very limited and a large part of the city's waste still found its way into the river Senne. The river carried waste and carrion and regularly overflowed, or dried out in the summer, leaving behind less-than-pleasant smells.\r\nIt was partially due to this, that the government in the second half of the 19th century decided to completely transform the Senne and its neighbouring streets by building great boulevards to cover the insalubrious area. Between the two world wars a second transformation: a portion of the Senne was diverted and then covered over. The sewerage network improved and grew over the years, going from 45 km in 1847 to the 350 km that we have today.\r\n The entrance to the museum is housed in one of the toll pavilions that used to collect taxes on goods that entered the city.","description_print":null,"booking_url":"https:\/\/www.ticketing.brussels\/en\/tickets\/event-details.Votre-entree-au-Musee-des-Egouts.535f21f8-15a3-4ee5-b242-a8dc5aed84e0","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e des \u00c9gouts - Mus\u00e9es de la Ville de Bruxelles","address_street_name":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedesegouts.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 83","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e des \u00c9gouts - Mus\u00e9es de la Ville de Bruxelles","address_street_name":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedesegouts.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 83","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e des \u00c9gouts","address_street_name":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedesegouts.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 83","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Au premier abord, on n\u2019y aurait pas pens\u00e9\u2026 Aller visiter les \u00e9gouts d\u2019une grande ville ? Mais en y r\u00e9fl\u00e9chissant un court instant, on per\u00e7oit vite l\u2019int\u00e9r\u00eat et les apprentissages potentiels ! Cet endroit qu\u2019aujourd\u2019hui on n\u2019imagine pas autrement qu\u2019enfoui\u2026 n\u2019a pas toujours exist\u00e9 sous cette forme, loin s\u2019en faut !\r\nC\u2019est au 17e si\u00e8cle que se met en place \u00e0 Bruxelles le premier r\u00e9seau d\u2019\u00e9gouts ; toutefois celui-ci reste \u00e9l\u00e9mentaire et bon nombre de d\u00e9chets terminent encore leur itin\u00e9raire dans le cours d\u2019eau bruxellois, la Senne. Celle-ci charrie d\u00e9tritus et charognes, et d\u00e9borde r\u00e9guli\u00e8rement en temps de pluie, ou s\u2019ass\u00e8che en \u00e9t\u00e9, laissant s\u2019\u00e9chapper des odeurs peu subtiles\u2026\r\nUn grand plan d\u2019assainissement est ex\u00e9cut\u00e9 dans la seconde moiti\u00e9 du 19e si\u00e8cle. On d\u00e9cide de vo\u00fbter la Senne et d\u2019\u00e9tablir de larges boulevards \u00e0 la place des ruelles insalubres. Durant l\u2019entre-deux-guerres, une deuxi\u00e8me entreprise de d\u00e9tournement et de vo\u00fbtement du cours d\u2019eau viendra renforcer l\u2019efficacit\u00e9 des premiers travaux.\r\nProgressivement, le r\u00e9seau des \u00e9gouts va se perfectionner et s\u2019agrandir : comptant 45 km en 1847, on d\u00e9nombre actuellement 350 km de d\u00e9dales souterrains, qui recueillent conjointement les eaux pluviales et les eaux us\u00e9es provenant de l\u2019activit\u00e9 humaine. \r\n\r\nAper\u00e7u de ce r\u00e9seau, explications sur son histoire et le travail des hommes qui l\u2019entretiennent, cycle de l\u2019eau, etc. : ce sont l\u00e0 quelques-unes des th\u00e9matiques qui vous y attendent ! Notez que l\u2019entr\u00e9e du mus\u00e9e si\u00e8ge dans un des deux \u00ab pavillons d\u2019octroi \u00bb, b\u00e2timents qui mat\u00e9rialisent la perception de la taxe sur tous les biens entrant dans la Ville au 19e si\u00e8cle.","description_print":null,"booking_url":"https:\/\/www.ticketing.brussels\/fr\/tickets\/event-details.Votre-entree-au-Musee-des-Egouts.535f21f8-15a3-4ee5-b242-a8dc5aed84e0","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"Museo del Alcantarillado (Mus\u00e9e des Egouts)","address_street_name":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museedesegouts.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 83","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Pavillons d\u2019Octroi, Porte d'Anderlecht","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"En un primer momento, a uno no se le pasar\u00eda por la cabeza... \u00bfIr a visitar las alcantarillas de una gran ciudad? Pero si te paras a pensarlo, \u00a1ver\u00e1s r\u00e1pidamente el potencial de aprendizaje y el inter\u00e9s! Este lugar que, actualmente, solo nos imaginamos bajo tierra no siempre lo ha estado, ni mucho menos. En el siglo XVII se cre\u00f3 el primer sistema de alcantarillado en Bruselas; sin embargo, segu\u00eda siendo b\u00e1sico y muchos residuos terminaban su recorrido en el r\u00edo de la ciudad, el Senne. Este r\u00edo, que llevaba basura y carro\u00f1a, se sol\u00eda desbordar normalmente en \u00e9poca de lluvias, o se secaba en verano, lo que hac\u00eda que desprendiera olores desagradables...\r\nEn la segunda mitad del siglo XIX se puso en marcha un importante plan de saneamiento.\r\nSe decidi\u00f3 recubrir el Senne y crear amplios bulevares en lugar de callejones insalubres. Durante el per\u00edodo de entreguerras, unas segundas obras de recubrimiento y desv\u00edo del agua reforzaron las primeras. Gradualmente, el sistema de alcantarillado se mejor\u00f3 y ampli\u00f3: de 45 km en 1847, actualmente hay 350 km de laberintos subterr\u00e1neos, que recogen conjuntamente el agua de lluvia y las aguas residuales de la ciudad. El museo se inaugur\u00f3 en 1988 como respuesta a una demanda creciente y ofrece visitas realizadas por el propio personal del Servicio de Alcantarillado. Gracias a este museo podr\u00e1s disfrutar de una perspectiva general de esta red, explicaciones sobre su historia y sobre la labor que desempe\u00f1an sus trabajadores, informaci\u00f3n sobre el ciclo hidrol\u00f3gico, etc. Cabe destacar que la entrada al museo se encuentra en uno de los dos Pavillons d\u2019octroi, los edificios donde se recaudaban los impuestos de todas las mercanc\u00edas que entraban en la ciudad en el siglo XIX.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"Riolenmuseum","address_street_name":"Octrooipaviljoen, Anderlechtsepoort","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"musea@brucity.be","website":"http:\/\/www.riolenmuseum.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 279 43 83","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Octrooipaviljoen, Anderlechtsepoort","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"Zet eens een bezoek aan de Brusselse riolen en het Riolenmuseum op het programma van een uitstap in Brussel! Apart, ongewoon en onverwacht, maar vooral interessant en allesbehalve saai is zo\u2019n afdaling in ondergronds Brussel, begeleid door ervaren stadsgidsen of (voormalige) rioolwerkers.\r\nRiolen zijn levensnoodzakelijk geworden voor onze manier van leven, vandaar dat we ons maar moeilijk kunnen voorstellen hoe het eraan toeging toen ze nog niet bestonden. Een bezoek aan het Riolenmuseum (en een echte riool!) is dan ook verrassend, ongewoon en ongemeen boeiend.\r\nIn de 17de eeuw werd in Brussel een eerste riolennet in gebruik genomen. Dat bleef nog erg beperkt en het overgrote deel van het afvalwater vond nog altijd zijn weg naar die ene Brusselse rivier, de Zenne. Die voerde dan ook een smurrie van afval, viezigheid en zelfs dierenkadavers de hele stad door. Als de Zenne bij overvloedige regen overstroomde of in volle zomer opdroogde in de zomer, zorgde dat natuurlijk voor weinig aangename geurtjes...\r\nGedeeltelijk omwille van die overlast besloot de overheid in de tweede helft van de 19de eeuw om een overwelving aan te brengen boven de Zenne en grote boulevards aan te leggen in plaats van de vieze en slordige steegjes. Later werd tussen de twee Wereldoorlogen nog een tweede keer ingegrepen: een deel van de Zenne werd verlegd en er werden nog meer overwelvingen aangebracht. \r\nLangzamerhand verbeterde en vergrootte het riolennet, van 45 km in 1847 naar de huidige 350 km riool, die zowel afval- als regenwater afvoert. \r\nNaast een bezoek aan de riolen zelf levert dit museum een schat aan boeiende en interessante informatie op over alle aspecten van riolen, rioolwater en de mensen die ze \u2013 vaak in gevaarlijke en altijd in onaangename omstandigheden - onderhouden. Leuk: de ingang van het museum is gehuisvest in een van de twee octrooipaviljoenen aan de Anderlechtse Poort, waar vroeger tol werd geheven op goederen die in de stad werden binnengebracht.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":"https:\/\/www.ticketing.brussels\/nl\/tickets\/event-details.Votre-entree-au-Musee-des-Egouts.535f21f8-15a3-4ee5-b242-a8dc5aed84e0","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"region":"brussels","backoffice_id":989,"location":{"lat":50.8450404,"lon":4.3386943},"last_updated_at":"2024-07-10T13:41:35+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:13:58+02:00","is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"resto_ranking":0},"media":[{"type":"photo","link":"https:\/\/agendabrussels2.imgix.net\/0c3444ec84f72e93aa20059425cf4a2905e53b5d.jpg","width":4032,"height":3024,"ratio":1.33,"oEmbed_height":3024,"oEmbed_width":4032,"translations":{"de":{"title":"\u00c0 la rencontre de nos voisins \u2013 Le Groene Phare","copyright":null},"pt":{"title":"\u00c0 la rencontre de nos voisins \u2013 Le Groene Phare","copyright":null},"en":{"title":"\u00c0 la rencontre de nos voisins \u2013 Le Groene Phare","copyright":null},"it":{"title":"\u00c0 la rencontre de nos voisins \u2013 Le Groene Phare","copyright":null},"cn":{"title":"\u00c0 la rencontre de nos voisins \u2013 Le Groene Phare","copyright":null},"fr":{"title":"\u00c0 la rencontre de nos voisins \u2013 Le Groene Phare","copyright":null},"sp":{"title":"\u00c0 la rencontre de nos voisins \u2013 Le Groene Phare","copyright":null},"nl":{"title":"\u00c0 la rencontre de nos voisins \u2013 Le Groene Phare","copyright":null}}}],"dates":[{"day":"2024-12-01","doors":"14:00:00","start":"14:00:00","end":"17:00:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2025-01-05","doors":"14:00:00","start":"14:00:00","end":"17:00:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2025-04-06","doors":"14:00:00","start":"14:00:00","end":"17:00:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2025-06-01","doors":"14:00:00","start":"14:00:00","end":"17:00:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false}],"prices":[],"date_exceptions":[],"closing_days":[],"child_events":[],"parent_events":[],"accessibilities":[],"recurring":[],"targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"educational_targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"tags":[]},{"id":5700002876,"date_start":"2024-10-19","date_end":"2025-04-19","date_next":"2025-01-05","accept_article27":true,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":true,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_pay_as_you_can":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"last_updated_at":"2025-01-05T01:01:44+01:00","published_at":"2024-10-22T16:57:48+02:00","publication_state":"public","date_embargo":null,"show_in_agenda":true,"is_outside":false,"is_high_capacity":false,"is_not_major_event":false,"backoffice_id":310245,"facebook_link":null,"import_origin":null,"is_part_of":null,"sub_type":"other","ranking":0.22191822427467614,"languages":{"spoken":["fr","nl","en"],"subtitles":[]},"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"de":"Ausstellung","pt":null,"en":"Exhibitions","it":"Esposizioni","cn":null,"fr":"Expositions","sp":"Exhibici\u00f3n","nl":"Tentoonstellingen"}},"others":{}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"Make a way for trees","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.autrique.be","email":"info@autrique.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700002876"},"pt":{"name":"Make a way for trees","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.autrique.be","email":"info@autrique.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700002876"},"en":{"name":"Make a way for trees","shortdescr":"Our intention is also to raise awareness of the actors and projects linked to the presence, management and preservation of this green heritage: a journey between the long history of nature and the short history of the house, and the relationship between human life and nature.\n","longdescr":"According to the latest data from Brussels Environment (2023), the Belgian capital is one of the greenest cities in Europe, with 1,036 accessible green spaces of all sizes. This represents to an area of 3,129 hectares, or around 20% of its surface area. \n\nThrough the Art Nouveau architectural elements of the Maison Autrique, a selection of artworks from the 19th and 20th century, some contemporary creations and contributions from historians and scientists, the 'Trees' exhibition illustrates the emergence of a new urban scenery. The Maison Autrique propose to analyse the transformation of the way we look at and relate to nature in recent periods of Schaerbeek's history. This exhibition is an opportunity to question the place of nature in the urban environment, to describe our experiences of nature in the city. Our intention is also to raise awareness of the actors and projects linked to the presence, management and preservation of this green heritage: a journey between the long history of nature and the short history of the house, and the relationship between human life and nature.\n\nBy studying the history of our green and majestic neighbours, we question our vision of nature in the 21st century. Make a way for trees!\n","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.autrique.be","email":"info@autrique.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700002876"},"it":{"name":"Make a way for trees","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.autrique.be","email":"info@autrique.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700002876"},"cn":{"name":"Make a way for trees","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.autrique.be","email":"info@autrique.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700002876"},"fr":{"name":"Place aux Arbres","shortdescr":"L'exposition est l\u2019occasion de questionner la place de la nature en milieu urbain et de d\u00e9crire nos exp\u00e9riences de celle-ci en ville. Nous voulons \u00e9galement mettre en avant les acteurs et projets li\u00e9s \u00e0 la pr\u00e9sence, \u00e0 la gestion et \u00e0 la sauvegarde de ce patrimoine vert : un parcours entre l\u2019histoire longue de la nature et l\u2019histoire courte de la maison, et le rapport entre vie humaine et nature.","longdescr":"Selon les derni\u00e8res donn\u00e9es de Bruxelles Environnement (2023), la capitale belge est l\u2019une des villes les plus v\u00e9g\u00e9tales d\u2019Europe avec 1.036 espaces verts accessibles, de toutes tailles confondues. Cela correspond \u00e0 une superficie de 3.129 hectares, soit environ 20% de sa surface. \n\nA travers les \u00e9l\u00e9ments architecturaux Art nouveau de la Maison Autrique, par le biais d\u2019une s\u00e9lection d\u2019\u0153uvres d\u2019art des 19e et 20e si\u00e8cles, de quelques cr\u00e9ations contemporaines et d\u2019interventions d\u2019historiens et de scientifiques, l\u2019exposition \u00ab Arbres \u00bb illustre l\u2019apparition d\u2019un nouveau d\u00e9cor urbain. La Maison Autrique propose d\u2019analyser la transformation du regard et du rapport \u00e0 la nature dans les p\u00e9riodes r\u00e9centes de l\u2019histoire schaerbeekoise. Cette exposition est l\u2019occasion de questionner la place de la nature en milieu urbain et de d\u00e9crire nos exp\u00e9riences de celle-ci en ville. Nous voulons \u00e9galement mettre en avant les acteurs et projets li\u00e9s \u00e0 la pr\u00e9sence, \u00e0 la gestion et \u00e0 la sauvegarde de ce patrimoine vert : un parcours entre l\u2019histoire longue de la nature et l\u2019histoire courte de la maison, et le rapport entre vie humaine et nature.\nPar l\u2019\u00e9tude de l\u2019histoire de nos voisins verts et majestueux, nous questionnons notre vision de la nature au 21e si\u00e8cle. Place aux arbres ! \n","performers":"Willem Battaille, Euphrosine Beernaert, Kikie Cr\u00eavecoeur, Gisbert Combaz, Joseph Coosemans, Dominique Discors, Gilbert Fastenaekens, Georges Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric, Nathalie Joiris, Jenos Kaparthy, Maurice Langaskens, Jacques Mathy, Maurice Minsart, Constant Montald, L\u00e9on Spilliaert, Henri Stiellemans, Taf Wallet, Albert Terken, Eug\u00e8ne Thelen, Victor Van Brabant,  Eug\u00e8ne Verboekhoven, Pascaline Wollast. \n","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.autrique.be","email":"info@autrique.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700002876"},"sp":{"name":"Make a way for trees","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.autrique.be","email":"info@autrique.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700002876"},"nl":{"name":"Ruimte voor bomen","shortdescr":"Deze tentoonstelling is een gelegenheid om de plaats van de natuur in de stedelijke omgeving in vraag te stellen, om onze ervaringen met de natuur in de stad te beschrijven. We willen ook een stem geven aan de actoren en projecten in verband met de aanwezigheid, het beheer en het behoud van dit groene erfgoed te sensibiliseren.\n","longdescr":"Volgens de laatste cijfers van Leefmilieu Brussel (2023) is de Belgische hoofdstad een van de groenste steden van Europa, met 1.036 toegankelijke groene ruimten van alle groottes. Dit komt overeen met een oppervlakte van 3.129 hectare, of ongeveer 20% van de oppervlakte. \n\nAan de hand van de architecturale Art Nouveau-elementen van het Autrique-huis zelf, een selectie kunstwerken uit de 19de en 20ste eeuw, enkele hedendaagse creaties en bijdragen van historici en wetenschappers, illustreert deze tentoonstelling de opkomst van een nieuwe stedelijke omgeving. Het Autrique huis stelt voor om te analyseren de transformatie van de manier waarop we naar de natuur kijken. Ons uitgangspunt is de snelle veranderende relatie met de natuur in recente periodes van de geschiedenis van Schaarbeek. Deze tentoonstelling is een gelegenheid om de plaats van de natuur in de stedelijke omgeving in vraag te stellen, om onze ervaringen met de natuur in de stad te beschrijven. We willen ook een stem geven aan de actoren en projecten in verband met de aanwezigheid, het beheer en het behoud van dit groene erfgoed te sensibiliseren: een reis tussen de lange geschiedenis van de natuur en de korte geschiedenis van het huis, en de relatie tussen het menselijk leven en de natuur.\n\nDoor de geschiedenis van onze groene en majestueuze buren te bestuderen, stellen we onze visie op de natuur in de 21e eeuw in vraag. Maak plaats voor de bomen!\n","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.autrique.be","email":"info@autrique.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700002876"}},"place":{"id":241931,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Maison Autrique","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht","address_street_number":"266","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autrique.be","website":"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/maisonautrique\/","phone_contact":"+32 2 215 66 00","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1030","address_city":"Schaerbeek","address_line1":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht, 266","address_line2":"1030 Schaerbeek","description_web":"Als erstes bedeutendes Bauwerk des Jugendstil-Architekten Victor Horta bildet das Maison Autrique ein wichtiges Element des Br\u00fcsseler Architekturerbes.\r\n\r\nEin Meilenstein der Br\u00fcsseler Architekturgeschichte: Denn das Geb\u00e4ude aus dem Jahr 1893 stellt eine wesentliche Etappe in der Entwicklung der gr\u00f6\u00dften belgischen Architekten dar. Durch das Geb\u00e4ude f\u00fchrt eine Szenographie, die von den beiden belgischen Comic-Gr\u00f6\u00dfen Fran\u00e7ois Schuiten und Beno\u00eet Peeter konzipiert wurde. Zugrundeliegende Idee war es, aus diesem Geb\u00e4ude eine Art \"Haus der H\u00e4user\" zu machen, eine Huldigung an die Br\u00fcsseler Architektur und zugleich ein Tor zum Imagin\u00e4ren.\r\n\r\nDas Maison Autrique bietet regelm\u00e4\u00dfig Ausstellungen rund um verschiedene Themen: das 19. Jahrhundert in Br\u00fcssel, Comic oder Jugenstil. ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Maison Autrique","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht","address_street_number":"266","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autrique.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autrique.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 215 66 00","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1030","address_city":"Schaerbeek","address_line1":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht, 266","address_line2":"1030 Schaerbeek","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Autrique House","address_street_name":"Haachtsesteenweg","address_street_number":"266","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autrique.be","website":"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/maisonautrique\/","phone_contact":"+32 2 215 66 00","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1030","address_city":"Schaerbeek","address_line1":"Haachtsesteenweg, 266","address_line2":"1030 Schaerbeek","description_web":"Maison Autrique is the very first striking building Victor Horta designed. It was built in 1893 and it's a major part of Brussels' architectural patrimonium. It underwent an exemplary restoration and is now open to the public. This house is an important Art Nouveau touchstone: we can already see elements that form a part of the continual explorations of the architect. It's interior division is full of surprises: Fran\u00e7ois Schuiten and Beno\u00eet Peeters have staged an original scenography, from the cellar to the attic. The house has thus become a sort of tribute to Brussels' private architecture, while at the same time tickling the imagination. The house hosts intimate concerts, temporary exhibitions and workshops for children.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Maison Autrique","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht","address_street_number":"266","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autrique.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autrique.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 215 66 00","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1030","address_city":"Schaerbeek","address_line1":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht, 266","address_line2":"1030 Schaerbeek","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Maison Autrique","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht","address_street_number":"266","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autrique.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autrique.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 215 66 00","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1030","address_city":"Schaerbeek","address_line1":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht, 266","address_line2":"1030 Schaerbeek","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Maison Autrique","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht","address_street_number":"266","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autrique.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autrique.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 215 66 00","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1030","address_city":"Schaerbeek","address_line1":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht, 266","address_line2":"1030 Schaerbeek","description_web":"La Maison Autrique (Horta 1893) est un jalon important de l'Art Nouveau. Elle a fait l'objet d'une restauration exemplaire. Ouverte au public, elle permet \u00e0 chacun de mieux saisir l'int\u00e9r\u00eat historique et esth\u00e9tique des vieilles demeures bruxelloises. Lors de votre visite, vous d\u00e9couvrirez des espaces d'exposition, une petite librairie th\u00e9matique et une sc\u00e9nographie originale sign\u00e9e Beno\u00eet Peeters et Fran\u00e7ois Schuiten. La maison accueille des petits concerts, des expositions temporaires et des ateliers pour enfants. ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"Casa Autrique","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht","address_street_number":"266","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autrique.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autrique.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 215 66 00","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1030","address_city":"Schaerbeek","address_line1":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht, 266","address_line2":"1030 Schaerbeek","description_web":"La casa Autrique, obra fundacional de Victor Horta, ha sido completamente renovada, con una puesta en escena imaginaria realizada por los guionistas y dibujantes Schuiten y Peeters. Al entrar, te sumerges en una atm\u00f3sfera \u00fanica.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"Autrique Huis","address_street_name":"Haachtsesteenweg","address_street_number":"266","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autrique.be","website":"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/maisonautrique\/","phone_contact":"+32 2 215 66 00","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1030","address_city":"Schaarbeek","address_line1":"Haachtsesteenweg, 266","address_line2":"1030 Schaarbeek","description_web":"Het Autrique Huis is het eerste markante gebouw van Victor Horta. Het werd in 1893 gebouwd en is nog steeds een voornaam element in het architectonisch patrimonium van Brussel. Het huis werd op uitmuntende wijze gerestaureerd en is open voor het publiek. Het huis is een belangrijke maatstaf van de Art Nouveau : men vindt er reeds elementen terug die de architect en zijn zoektocht kenmerken. De manier waarop de ruimte ingedeeld is, staat garant voor verrassingen : Fran\u00e7ois Schuiten en Beno\u00eet Peeters hebben een originele enscenering opgezet, waarbij het huis van de kelder tot de zolder ingericht werd. Zodoende wordt het huis een soort van eerbetoon aan de Brusselse priv\u00e9-architectuur, terwijl het ook de verbeelding aanspreekt. Het huis organiseert intieme concerten, tentoonstellingen en workshops voor kinderen.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"districts":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"zones":{"list":[20],"translations":{"de":["Norden"],"pt":[null],"en":["North"],"it":["Nord"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Nord"],"sp":["Norte"],"nl":["Noord"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":4383,"location":{"lat":50.8632575,"lon":4.3731694},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2024-09-10T13:09:05+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:17:19+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":241931,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Maison Autrique","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht","address_street_number":"266","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autrique.be","website":"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/maisonautrique\/","phone_contact":"+32 2 215 66 00","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1030","address_city":"Schaerbeek","address_line1":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht, 266","address_line2":"1030 Schaerbeek","description_web":"Als erstes bedeutendes Bauwerk des Jugendstil-Architekten Victor Horta bildet das Maison Autrique ein wichtiges Element des Br\u00fcsseler Architekturerbes.\r\n\r\nEin Meilenstein der Br\u00fcsseler Architekturgeschichte: Denn das Geb\u00e4ude aus dem Jahr 1893 stellt eine wesentliche Etappe in der Entwicklung der gr\u00f6\u00dften belgischen Architekten dar. Durch das Geb\u00e4ude f\u00fchrt eine Szenographie, die von den beiden belgischen Comic-Gr\u00f6\u00dfen Fran\u00e7ois Schuiten und Beno\u00eet Peeter konzipiert wurde. Zugrundeliegende Idee war es, aus diesem Geb\u00e4ude eine Art \"Haus der H\u00e4user\" zu machen, eine Huldigung an die Br\u00fcsseler Architektur und zugleich ein Tor zum Imagin\u00e4ren.\r\n\r\nDas Maison Autrique bietet regelm\u00e4\u00dfig Ausstellungen rund um verschiedene Themen: das 19. Jahrhundert in Br\u00fcssel, Comic oder Jugenstil. ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Maison Autrique","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht","address_street_number":"266","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autrique.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autrique.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 215 66 00","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1030","address_city":"Schaerbeek","address_line1":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht, 266","address_line2":"1030 Schaerbeek","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Autrique House","address_street_name":"Haachtsesteenweg","address_street_number":"266","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autrique.be","website":"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/maisonautrique\/","phone_contact":"+32 2 215 66 00","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1030","address_city":"Schaerbeek","address_line1":"Haachtsesteenweg, 266","address_line2":"1030 Schaerbeek","description_web":"Maison Autrique is the very first striking building Victor Horta designed. It was built in 1893 and it's a major part of Brussels' architectural patrimonium. It underwent an exemplary restoration and is now open to the public. This house is an important Art Nouveau touchstone: we can already see elements that form a part of the continual explorations of the architect. It's interior division is full of surprises: Fran\u00e7ois Schuiten and Beno\u00eet Peeters have staged an original scenography, from the cellar to the attic. The house has thus become a sort of tribute to Brussels' private architecture, while at the same time tickling the imagination. The house hosts intimate concerts, temporary exhibitions and workshops for children.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Maison Autrique","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht","address_street_number":"266","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@autrique.be","website":"http:\/\/www.autrique.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 215 66 00","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1030","address_city":"Schaerbeek","address_line1":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht, 266","address_line2":"1030 Schaerbeek","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Maison Autrique","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Haecht","address_street_number":"266","address_street_box":null,"email":"i