rs"],"it":["Visite guidate all\u2019interno"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Visites guid\u00e9es d\u2019int\u00e9rieurs"],"sp":["Visitas guiadas en espacios interiores"],"nl":["Interieur rondleidingen"]}}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"Guided tour of Haerens Hotel","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700004444"},"pt":{"name":"Guided tour of Haerens Hotel","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700004444"},"en":{"name":"Guided tour of Haerens Hotel","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"In 1928, the Art Deco architect Antoine Courtens was involved in two major projects: \u201cLe Palais de la Folle Chanson\u201d in Ixelles and this house for the engineer Robert Haerens and his wife, the sculptor Luisa Robelus. The Haerens building includes two separate apartments, each with its own entrance. The main apartment is on the first floor with a monumental entrance on Avenue Brugmann, and a central, circular reception hall, topped with a glass cupola which allows daylight to flood into the centre of the apartment. As always in the buildings of Antoine Courtens, the finishes are very sophisticated, such as the cutting and arrangement of marble and the wrought-ironwork designed by the architect. The facades of the building were recently restored and today it is used as offices.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/en\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700004444"},"it":{"name":"Guided tour of Haerens Hotel","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700004444"},"cn":{"name":"Guided tour of Haerens Hotel","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700004444"},"fr":{"name":"Visite guid\u00e9e de l'H\u00f4tel Haerens","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"En 1928, l'architecte Art d\u00e9co Antoine Courtens mena de front deux projets d'ampleur: la construction du Palais de la Folle Chanson \u00e0 Ixelles et la construction de l'H\u00f4tel Haerens pour l'ing\u00e9nieur Robert Haerens et son \u00e9pouse, la sculptrice Luisa Robelus. Le programme pr\u00e9voyait deux logements distincts, avec entr\u00e9es s\u00e9par\u00e9es. L'appartement principal, \u00e0 l'\u00e9tage, avec son entr\u00e9e monumentale avenue Brugmann, comprenait un hall de r\u00e9ception central et circulaire, coiff\u00e9 d'une coupole laissant p\u00e9n\u00e9trer la lumi\u00e8re naturelle au c\u0153ur de l'appartement. Comme toujours chez Antoine Courtens, les finitions sont tr\u00e8s soign\u00e9es: d\u00e9coupe et agencement des marbres, ferroneries ouvrag\u00e9es dessin\u00e9es par l'architecte... Le b\u00e2timent est aujourd'hui occup\u00e9 par des bureaux.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700004444"},"sp":{"name":"Guided tour of Haerens Hotel","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700004444"},"nl":{"name":"Rondleiding van het Haerens Herenhuis","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"In 1928 voert de art deco-architect Antoine Courtens twee grote projecten tegelijk uit: de bouw van het Palais de la Folle Chanson in Elsene en de bouw van hotel Haerens voor de ingenieur Robert Haerens en zijn echtgenote, de beeldhouwster Luisa Robelus. Het programma bestaat uit twee woningen met aparte ingangen. Het hoofdappartement op de bovenverdieping, met monumentale ingang aan de Brugmannlaan, bestaat uit een centrale, ronde ontvangsthal, met een koepel die het natuurlijk licht binnenlaat in het hart van het appartement. Zoals altijd bij Antoine Courtens is de afwerking uiterst verzorgd: de uitsnijdingen en opbouw van het marmer, het fijn siersmeedwerk dat door de architect getekend werd... Het gebouw, waarvan de gevel onlangs werd gerestaureerd, huisvest momenteel kantoren.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/nl\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700004444"}},"place":{"id":280019,"translations":{"de":{"name":"H\u00f4tel Haerens","address_street_name":"Avenue Brugmann","address_street_number":"384","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Avenue Brugmann, 384","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"H\u00f4tel Haerens","address_street_name":"Avenue Brugmann","address_street